  "input": {
    "question": "LIBRETTO-001의 코호트별 ORR, 보고된 분모와 결측을 분리해 검토하라. 이 발췌만으로 용량 간 비교가 가능한가?",
    "asset": "selpercatinib",
    "indication": "RET fusion-positive thyroid cancer",
    "study": "LIBRETTO-001",
    "spans": [
      {
        "id": "fda-0",
        "source_digest": "89cb0ce158a97d4b70fb19e6a8c38211b61a2cecd2d51613e009f9d51244a383",
        "page": null,
        "text": "On June 12, 2024, the Food and Drug Administration granted traditional approval to selpercatinib (Retevmo, Eli Lilly and Company) for adult and pediatric patients 2 years of age and older with advanced or metastatic RET fusion-positive thyroid cancer who require systemic therapy and who are radioactive iodine-refractory (if radioactive iodine is appropriate).",
        "locator": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/fda-approves-selpercatinib-ret-fusion-positive-thyroid-cancer · selpercatinib-fda-2024/1 · selected paragraph 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "fda-1",
        "source_digest": "89cb0ce158a97d4b70fb19e6a8c38211b61a2cecd2d51613e009f9d51244a383",
        "page": null,
        "text": "Efficacy was evaluated in LIBRETTO-001 (NCT03157128), a multicenter, open-label, muti-cohort clinical trial in 65 patients with RET fusion-positive thyroid cancer who were radioactive iodine (RAI)-refractory (if RAI was an appropriate treatment option) and were systemic therapy naïve and patients who were previously treated, in separate cohorts.",
        "locator": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/fda-approves-selpercatinib-ret-fusion-positive-thyroid-cancer · selpercatinib-fda-2024/1 · selected paragraph 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "fda-2",
        "source_digest": "89cb0ce158a97d4b70fb19e6a8c38211b61a2cecd2d51613e009f9d51244a383",
        "page": null,
        "text": "The major efficacy outcome measures were overall response rate (ORR) and duration of response (DOR). The ORR was 85% (95% CI: 71%, 94%) in the 41 previously treated patients and 96% (95% CI: 79%, 100%) in the 24 systemic therapy naïve patients. Median DOR was 26.7 months (95% CI: 12.1, not evaluable [NE]) in the previously treated patients and NE (95% CI: 42.8, NE) in the systemic therapy naïve patients.",
        "locator": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/fda-approves-selpercatinib-ret-fusion-positive-thyroid-cancer · selpercatinib-fda-2024/1 · selected paragraph 3"
      },
      {
        "id": "fda-3",
        "source_digest": "89cb0ce158a97d4b70fb19e6a8c38211b61a2cecd2d51613e009f9d51244a383",
        "page": null,
        "text": "Supportive evidence included ORR and DOR data from 10 pediatric and young adult patients with RET fusion-positive thyroid cancer treated in Study LIBRETTO-121 (J2G-OX-JZJJ; NCT03899792), an international, single-arm, multi-cohort clinical trial of selpercatinib in pediatric and young adult patients with advanced RET-altered solid tumors. The ORR was 60% (95% CI: 26%, 88%), and 83% had an observed duration of response ≥ 12 months.",
        "locator": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/fda-approves-selpercatinib-ret-fusion-positive-thyroid-cancer · selpercatinib-fda-2024/1 · selected paragraph 4"
      },
      {
        "id": "fda-4",
        "source_digest": "89cb0ce158a97d4b70fb19e6a8c38211b61a2cecd2d51613e009f9d51244a383",
        "page": null,
        "text": "The recommended selpercatinib dose for pediatric patients 2 to less than 12 years of age is based on body surface area. It is based on weight for patients 12 years of age and older. See the prescribing information for specific dosing information.",
        "locator": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/fda-approves-selpercatinib-ret-fusion-positive-thyroid-cancer · selpercatinib-fda-2024/1 · selected paragraph 5"
      }
    ],
